It is very interesting to go to nethack.wikia.com and read the
excellent descriptions of each version.  3.1 was a massive revision to
the game, and changes have been relatively slight since then.  Many of
the things that people see as essential to the game were introduced
there, and players before did without them just fine.

> Or whether its power should be reduced at all.

Well I was responding to the original post, see.


> If you reduce its power, you reduce its utility for ALL roles.  I use
> Cure Sickness as an excellent example here -- for roles who have skill
> in Healing spells, Cure Sickness is a better solution to "Ill" than a
> unicorn horn, because it works 100% of the time on something that's
> fatal if you don't fix it.  But not many roles have skill in Healing,
> and Ill is a pretty critical problem.  If a unicorn horn is nerfed too
> much for those roles, we are basically saying "you'll end up using the
> big healing potions or dying", and that's not good; what if they don't
> find the big healing potions or burn them up earlier?

Cure Sickness is the big thing that makes a unicorn essential, as in,
magic resistance-type essential.  However, even other roles don't NEED
it; uncursed or better potions of extra healing or full healing both
infallibly cure sickness.  Reducing the power of unicorn horns also
has the side effect of making those potions more
useful, see.


> Consider this simple change to the unicorn horn for a moment:  What if
> you could only fix bad status effects by (a)pplying it while it was wielded?

Not a useful distinction, it just takes one more turn to get whatever
long-lasting or quasi-permanent condition fixed.


> Consider also another change:  What if there were a "generalist" spell
> skill that every role could get at least "basic" in... into which such
> spells as Detect Foot, Cure Blindness, and Cure Sickness might fall?

Isn't there already something like that in the code?  Some are
considered emergency spells, and there is a casting bonus for those.


